 as the first case, with the full ordering, the before/after behaviour, and each file's role.\n\nTwo things worth flagging, both left as-is since they're outside what you asked for:\n\n- `case-closed` has the earliest deadline in the file (2026-08-24) but is correctly excluded by status. That looks deliberate in the fixture — it means a filter bug would be visible in the output, not masked by the ordering.\n- `handoff.py:4` does `from queue import ordered_open_cases`, and `queue` is a Python standard-library module name. It resolves to the local file here because the script's own directory sits ahead of the stdlib on `sys.path`, so the checks pass — but the shadowing is fragile if this code is ever imported from another working directory. Renaming the module would fix it if you want that cleaned up.","ttft_ms":2215,"ttft_stream_ms":1955,"time_to_request_ms":71,"type":"result","duration_ms":39737,"uuid":"0e9921dd-d1b7-4d3d-a210-2a3daeb6693d"}
